Here's a simple Nginx config to get your Node.js app running:

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name your-domain.com;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://localhost:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
    }
}
```

This forwards HTTP traffic from port 80 to your Node process on port 3000. Once you're ready for HTTPS, let me know and I can share the SSL config.
